%N A399602 The first 25 prime numbers (from 2 to 97) arranged row by row into a 5 X 5 balanced quasi-magic square. Every outer row and column sums to 215, while the four lines passing through the central number 2 (central row, central column, and both diagonals) sum exactly to 200.
%F A399602 The matrix row sums are M_1 = M_2 = M_4 = M_5 = 215, and M_3 = 200. The column sums are C_1 = C_2 = C_4 = C_5 = 215, and C_3 = 200. The main diagonal and anti-diagonal sums are both exactly 200. This configuration represents the unique fundamental solution (up to border permutations) for this set of primes. Verified via exhaustive computational search.
%e A399602 The 25 initial terms correspond to the following 5 X 5 quasi-magic square layout (read row by row):
%e A399602    7   47   89   29   43  -> Row 1 sums to 215
%e A399602   11   53   31   59   61  -> Row 2 sums to 215
%e A399602   97   79    2   19    3  -> Row 3 sums to 200 (with 2 at the center)
%e A399602   17   13   73   71   41  -> Row 4 sums to 215
%e A399602   83   23    5   37   67  -> Row 5 sums to 215
%e A399602 The four lines passing through the center (row 3, column 3, main diagonal, and antidiagonal) all sum exactly to 200.
